{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1474263-exalted-isekai-or-we-re-trapped-in-the-hyborian-age-only-there-s-mecha","id":1474263,"title":"Exalted Isekai or, \"We're trapped in the Hyborian Age, only there's mecha.\"","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-02-09T00:45:50-08:00","id":1474263,"title":"Exalted Isekai or, \"We're trapped in the Hyborian Age, only there's mecha.\"","content":"My players are set in their ways and getting them to try out anything other than the World of Darkness is something that I often struggle with. I've tried and failed to get them into Exalted but the lore is simply too daunting for them so I was thinking of trying something new: Ikekai Exalted.<br /> <br /> The premise is that their characters in the World of Darkness make a deal with a mysterious entity to not die (or whatever Maguffin I make) and are mentally hurled back in time to what they perceive as the distant past. They are each in the body of a recently slain Exalted and must learn the history, mythology, etcetera-etcetera of the setting while carrying out their quest for the Entity.<br /> <br /> (I'm thinking its secretly the Maiden of Endings)<br /> <br /> Given their love of the World of Darkness, I'm thinking of playing up the connections but also making them more than a little nonsensical. Like they'll come across a city-state named Enoch and find it ruled by an Abyssal named Kane and his wife Zillah, general Irad, and son Enoch. However, they're definitely not vampires and a lot better than the demon-worshipers outside the city.<br /> <br /> Stuff like that.<br /> <br /> Plus there's also the fact the universe bears no resemblance to the physics of their world. I'm talking full flat-Earth, sun is a giant mech, and so on. I may have the players wonder if they're in a Paradox Realm (assuming they start as mages) or mass hallucination.<br /> <br /> What do you think?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-09T01:51:57-08:00","id":1474269,"title":"","content":"As you can guess this probably won't be the most serious of games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-09T04:09:46-08:00","id":1474274,"title":"","content":"Well, if part of the issue is the lore being daunting to them, i would say gank the lore by throwing them in podunk, homebrew and inserting lore by bits in a &quot;need to, for advancing the story&quot; basis, but whatever, isekai can be fun too and let's them start from a perspective they are more familiar &amp; confortable with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1474263-exalted-isekai-or-we-re-trapped-in-the-hyborian-age-only-there-s-mecha#post1474263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given their love of the World of Darkness, I'm thinking of playing up the connections but also making them more than a little nonsensical. Like they'll come across a city-state named Enoch and find it ruled by an Abyssal named Kane and his wife Zillah, general Irad, and son Enoch. However, they're definitely not vampires and a lot better than the demon-worshipers outside the city.</div> </div> </div> </div>What, no Lilith?! Prepare to be FULL MOONED!!! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But on a more serious note, i would suggest you pick bits of cWoD lore to riff (and twist) according to what the PCs past lives were or vice-versa, ergo, lots of Book of Nod references make a fair bit of sense and can be quite engaging if they were cainites or even demons from Fallen - for ex-Garou or Awakened with their own peculiar cosmologies, much less so.<br /> <br /> So taking a little time to define what they were before incarnating as exalts in Creation - and how much impact those past lives will have or not in their capacities, knowledge or just color their perspectives as strangers in a strange land, is quite relevant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[